        "description": "Wave slope describes an aspect of sea surface wave geometry related to sea surface roughness. Mean square slope describes a derivation over multiple waves within a sea-state, for example calculated from moments of the wave directional spectrum. The phrase \"y_slope\" indicates that slope values are derived from vector components along the grid y-axis.",
        "canonical_units": "1",
        "cf-name": "sea_surface_wave_mean_square_y_slope",
        "type": [
          "wcrp:standard-name",
