        "description": "A velocity is a vector quantity. \"y\" indicates a vector component along the grid x-axis, positive with increasing y. The Stokes drift velocity is the average velocity when following a specific fluid parcel as it travels with the fluid flow. For instance, a particle floating at the free surface of water waves, experiences a net Stokes drift velocity in the direction of wave propagation.",
        "canonical_units": "m s-1",
        "cf-name": "sea_surface_wave_stokes_drift_y_velocity",
