        "ui-label": "Tendency Of Middle Atmosphere Moles Of Carbon Monoxide",
        "description": "\"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time.  \"middle_atmosphere_moles_of_X\" means the total number of moles of X contained in the troposphere and stratosphere, i.e, summed over that part of the atmospheric column and over the entire globe.  The chemical formula of carbon monoxide is CO.",
        "canonical_units": "mol s-1",
        "cf-name": "tendency_of_middle_atmosphere_moles_of_carbon_monoxide",
        "type": [
