      {
        "id": "tendency-of-sea-ice-amount-due-to-congelation-ice-accumulation",
        "validation-key": "tendency-of-sea-ice-amount-due-to-congelation-ice-accumulation",
        "ui-label": "Tendency Of Sea Ice Amount Due To Congelation Ice Accumulation",
        "description": "The phrase \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. \"Amount\" means mass per unit area. \"Sea ice\" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs. The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"Congelation ice\" means the freezing of sea water onto the underside of thin, new sea ice that has been formed by small areas of frazil ice crystals joining together into a continuous layer at the sea surface. Congelation ice forms under calm water conditions; it thickens and stabilizes the layer of sea ice and produces a smooth bottom surface.",
        "canonical_units": "kg m-2 s-1",
        "cf-name": "tendency_of_sea_ice_amount_due_to_congelation_ice_accumulation",
        "type": [
          "wcrp:standard-name",
          "cf"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tendency-of-sea-ice-amount-due-to-conversion-of-snow-to-sea-ice",
        "validation-key": "tendency-of-sea-ice-amount-due-to-conversion-of-snow-to-sea-ice",
        "ui-label": "Tendency Of Sea Ice Amount Due To Conversion Of Snow To Sea Ice",
        "description": "The phrase \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. \"Amount\" means mass per unit area. \"Sea ice\" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs. The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"Conversion of snow to sea ice\" occurs when the mass of snow accumulated on an area of sea ice is sufficient to cause the ice to become mostly submerged. Waves can then wash over the ice and snow surface and freeze into a layer that becomes \"snow ice\".",
        "canonical_units": "kg m-2 s-1",
        "cf-name": "tendency_of_sea_ice_amount_due_to_conversion_of_snow_to_sea_ice",
        "type": [
          "wcrp:standard-name",
          "cf"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tendency-of-sea-ice-amount-due-to-frazil-ice-accumulation-in-leads",
        "validation-key": "tendency-of-sea-ice-amount-due-to-frazil-ice-accumulation-in-leads",
        "ui-label": "Tendency Of Sea Ice Amount Due To Frazil Ice Accumulation In Leads",
        "description": "The phrase \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. \"Amount\" means mass per unit area. \"Sea ice\" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs. The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \"Frazil\" consists of needle like crystals of ice, typically between three and four millimeters in diameter, which form as sea water begins to freeze. Salt is expelled during the freezing process and frazil ice consists of nearly pure fresh water. Leads are stretches of open water within wider areas of sea ice.",
        "canonical_units": "kg m-2 s-1",
        "cf-name": "tendency_of_sea_ice_amount_due_to_frazil_ice_accumulation_in_leads",
        "type": [
          "wcrp:standard-name",
          "cf"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "tendency-of-sea-ice-amount-due-to-lateral-growth-of-ice-floes",
        "validation-key": "tendency-of-sea-ice-amount-due-to-lateral-growth-of-ice-floes",
        "ui-label": "Tendency Of Sea Ice Amount Due To Lateral Growth Of Ice Floes",
        "description": "The phrase \"tendency_of_X\" means derivative of X with respect to time. \"Amount\" means mass per unit area. \"Sea ice\" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs. The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. An ice floe is a flat expanse of sea ice, generally taken to be less than 10 km across. \"Lateral growth of ice floe\" means the accumulation of ice at the extreme edges of the ice area.",
        "canonical_units": "kg m-2 s-1",
        "cf-name": "tendency_of_sea_ice_amount_due_to_lateral_growth_of_ice_floes",
        "type": [
          "wcrp:standard-name",
          "cf"
