        "ui-label": "Troposphere Mole Content Of Iodine Monoxide",
        "description": "\"Content\" indicates a quantity per unit area. The \"troposphere content\" of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the tropopause. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used. The chemical formula for iodine_monoxide is IO.",
        "canonical_units": "mol m-2",
        "cf-name": "troposphere_mole_content_of_iodine_monoxide",
